<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00511.html">
<title>DSA-6592-1 chromium - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00511.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-28</dc:date>
<description>Security issues were discovered in Chromium which could result
in the execution of arbitrary code, denial of service, or information
disclosure.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6592-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6592-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00510.html">
<title>DSA-6591-1 openjdk-25 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00510.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-28</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the OpenJDK Java runtime,
which may result in denial of service, sandbox breakout, incomplete
certificate checks or information disclosure.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6591-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6591-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00509.html">
<title>DSA-6590-1 firefox-esr - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00509.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-28</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security issues have been found in the Mozilla Firefox web
browser, which could potentially result in the execution of arbitrary
code, sandbox escape, bypass of the same-origin policy, privilege
escalation, information disclosure or spoofing.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6590-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6590-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00505.html">
<title>DSA-6585-2 thunderbird - regression update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00505.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-27</dc:date>
<description>The update for thunderbird in DSA-6585-1 introduced a regression in
the supported for PGP-encrypted emails. Updated packages are now
available to correct this issue.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6585-2&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6585-2&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00508.html">
<title>DSA-6589-1 php-mongodb - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00508.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-27</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security vulnerabilities have been discovered in the MongoDB
driver for PHP, which could result in denial of service.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6589-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6589-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00507.html">
<title>DSA-6588-1 openjdk-21 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00507.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-27</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the OpenJDK Java runtime,
which may result in denial of service, sandbox bypass, incomplete
certificate checks or information disclosure.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6588-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6588-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00506.html">
<title>DSA-6587-1 pdns - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00506.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-27</dc:date>
<description>It was discovered that incorrect parsing of packets with compression
pointers in the PowerDNS DNS server could result in denial of service.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6587-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6587-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00504.html">
<title>DSA-6586-1 valkey - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00504.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-27</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities were discovered in Valkey, an in-memory key-value
database. These issues could cause denial of service and, in some cases,
potentially allow arbitrary code execution.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6586-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6586-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00503.html">
<title>DSA-6585-1 thunderbird - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00503.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-25</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security issues were discovered in Thunderbird, which could
result in the execution of arbitrary code or information disclosure
&lt;p&gt;
Debian follows the Thunderbird upstream releases. Support for the 140.x
series has ended, so starting with this update we&apos;re now following the
153.x series.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6585-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6585-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00502.html">
<title>DSA-6584-1 varnish - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00502.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-25</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities were discovered in Varnish Cache, an HTTP
accelerator, which could result in cache poisoning, authentication bypass
or denial of service.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-34475
&lt;p&gt;
    Tom Kinnaird discovered a deficiency in the parsing of HTTP/1.1
    absolute-form request targets. If the request URL is passed unchecked
    to a backend which accepts absolute-form URIs, a remote attacker
    could potentially poison the cache or bypass authentication. The
    issue affects requests for root URLs.                                                                               
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-93894
&lt;p&gt;
    Tristan Madani discovered a workspace buffer overflow in the .upper()
    and .lower() string methods of the Varnish Configuration Language.
    A remote attacker with knowledge of the active configuration could
    craft a request which exhausts the remaining workspace during case
    conversion, causing the worker process to crash and restart,
    resulting in denial of service. Exploitation depends on the
    configuration using these methods on attacker-controlled strings
    and on the applicable request size limits.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6584-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6584-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00499.html">
<title>DSA-6583-1 libheif - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00499.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-24</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security issues were discovered in libheif, a library for reading
and writing HEIF and AVIF images. Processing specially crafted images
could result in denial of service through excessive resource consumption
or crashes, or disclosure of process memory. A use-after-free and
double-free affecting timestamp handling during image encoding, including
transcoding of crafted images, is also addressed.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6583-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6583-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00498.html">
<title>DSA-6582-1 brotli - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00498.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-23</dc:date>
<description>A vulnerability was discovered in Brotli, a generic-purpose lossless
compression suite, which could result in denial of service, or
potentially the execution of arbitrary code.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6582-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6582-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00497.html">
<title>DSA-6581-1 unbound - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00497.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-23</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security vulnerabilities were discovered in Unbound, a validating,
recursive, caching DNS resolver.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-35501
&lt;p&gt;
    (DNSSEC) Bypass of a configured island trust anchor underneath an insecure
    parent from an attacker-controlled NSEC record.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-50106
&lt;p&gt;
    (DNSSEC) Possible insecure NXDOMAIN for non-existing records under a
    configured island trust anchor underneath an insecure parent.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-96405
&lt;p&gt;
    Aggregate DNS name chained pointer decompression work leads to degradation
    of service.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-97206
&lt;p&gt;
    DNS-over-QUIC path-migration can lead to use-after-free on multi-threaded
    deployments, leading to potential denial of service.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-109125
&lt;p&gt;
    Possible cache poisoning vulnerability via a cache side-channel exposed by
    &apos;unwanted-reply-threshold&apos;.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6581-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6581-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00496.html">
<title>DSA-6580-1 erlang - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00496.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-23</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities were discovered in Erlang/OTP, a programming
language and runtime environment. These issues could result in denial of
service, HTTP request smuggling, or bypass of authentication and access
restrictions, including TLS server impersonation.
&lt;p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
The affected components include the HTTP client and server, SSH, TLS,
ASN.1 decoding, the network driver, and URI, LDAP and SNMP parsing. The
update tightens protocol validation and HTTP/SSH resource limits.
Applications relying on previously permissive behavior may need
adjustment.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6580-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6580-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00495.html">
<title>DSA-6579-1 roundcube - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00495.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-23</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities were discovered in roundcube, a skinnable AJAX
based webmail solution for IMAP servers, which could result in IMAP
command injection, cross-site scripting, SSRF bypass, email header
injection, css property injection, remote content blocking bypass,
information disclosure or privilege escalation.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6579-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6579-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00494.html">
<title>DSA-6578-1 aide - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00494.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-22</dc:date>
<description>Two vulnerabilities were discovered in aide, an advanced intrusion
detection system, which could allow a local user to bypass the detection
of malicious files.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6578-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6578-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00493.html">
<title>DSA-6577-1 chromium - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00493.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-22</dc:date>
<description>Security issues were discovered in Chromium which could result
in the execution of arbitrary code, denial of service, or information
disclosure.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6577-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6577-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00492.html">
<title>DSA-6534-3 webkit2gtk - regression update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00492.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-22</dc:date>
<description>The webkit2gtk update released as DSA-6534-1 introduced a regression
that prevents Evolution from displaying images embedded in HTML
emails.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6534-3&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6534-3&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00491.html">
<title>DSA-6576-1 bind9 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00491.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-21</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities were discovered in BIND, a DNS server
implementation, which could result in denial of service or remote code
execution.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6576-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6576-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00490.html">
<title>DSA-6575-1 nginx - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00490.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-21</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities were discovered in nginx, a high performance web
and reverse proxy server. Depending on the configuration, these could
result in memory corruption, denial of service, injection of requests to
backend servers, or bypass of client certificate authentication.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-15176
&lt;p&gt;
    Mapping a rewritten request URI to a filesystem path in a location
    using the alias directive could cause a buffer overflow.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-93479
&lt;p&gt;
    Evaluation of string expressions in the HTTP and stream modules
    could overwrite reserved buffer space, resulting in a buffer overflow.
    Affected operations include evaluation of variable document roots
    and access log paths.
&lt;p&gt;
    The affected code was introduced into the trixie package by an earlier
    security backport.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-95101
&lt;p&gt;
    Incorrect handling of fragmented unknown HTTP/3 frames could cause
    their contents to be treated as request body data. When proxying
    requests, this could allow injection of requests into a backend server
    or bypass of request body size limits.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-97205
&lt;p&gt;
    A counter tracking pending asynchronous operations could overflow,
    causing request memory to be freed while still in use. This
    use-after-free could result in memory corruption or denial of service.
&lt;p&gt;
CVE-2026-97629
&lt;p&gt;
    Incomplete synchronisation of TLS session ticket keys between worker
    processes could leave a worker using uninitialised key material. This
    could allow forged TLS sessions and bypass of client certificate
    authentication.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6575-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6575-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00489.html">
<title>DSA-6574-1 php8.4 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00489.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-21</dc:date>
<description>It was discovered that incorrect memory state tracking in PHP, a
widely-used open source general purpose scripting language, could
result in the execution of arbitrary code.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6574-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6574-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00488.html">
<title>DSA-6573-1 firefox-esr - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00488.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-21</dc:date>
<description>This update blocks compromised intermediate certificates issued by the
eMudhra CA.
&lt;p&gt;
Most users will have these certs already blocked by the OneCRL feature
provided by Firefox. This update blocks the certificates also for
installations which have RemoteSettings disabled or which are unable to
connect to the revocation backend service due to network constraints.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6573-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6573-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00487.html">
<title>DSA-6572-1 ca-certificates - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00487.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-20</dc:date>
<description>It was discovered that several eMudhra intermediate CA certificates have
been compromised. Updated ca-certificate packages are provided to remove
the &quot;emSign ECC Root CA - G3&quot; and &quot;Comodo AAA Services root&quot;
certificates.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6572-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6572-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00486.html">
<title>DSA-6571-1 xen - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00486.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-18</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities have been discovered in the Xen hypervisor,
which could result in privilege escalation, information disclosure or
denial of service.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6571-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6571-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00485.html">
<title>DSA-6570-1 haproxy - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00485.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-18</dc:date>
<description>Two vulnerabilities were discovered in HAProxy, a fast and reliable load
balancing reverse proxy, which could result in denial of service.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6570-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6570-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00484.html">
<title>DSA-6567-2 cifs-utils - regression update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00484.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-18</dc:date>
<description>The update for cifs-utils announced in DSA 6567-1 introduced a
regression when using the sec=krb5 and cruid mount options. Updated
packages are now available to correct this issue.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6567-2&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6567-2&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00483.html">
<title>DSA-6569-1 apache2 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00483.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-16</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities have been discovered in the Apache HTTP server,
which may result in denial of service, information disclosure,
authentication bypass or HTTP request smuggling.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6569-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6569-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00482.html">
<title>DSA-6568-1 linux - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00482.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-16</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the Linux kernel that
may lead to a privilege escalation, denial of service or information
leaks.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6568-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6568-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00481.html">
<title>DSA-6567-1 cifs-utils - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00481.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-16</dc:date>
<description>Two vulnerabilities were discovered in cifs-utils, the Common Internet
File System utilities, which could result in privilege escalation.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6567-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6567-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00480.html">
<title>DSA-6566-1 expat - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00480.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-10-16</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in Expat, an XML parsing C
library, which could result in denial of service or potentially the
execution of arbitrary code, if a malformed XML file is processed.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6566-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6566-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
</rdf:RDF>
